  "script": "Apple's third beta of iOS twenty seven point two just dropped, and the biggest change you'll notice is a battery icon. That's a clue to when you'll get the update.\n\nThe big features of twenty seven point two already landed in beta one: the new Health app, and Siri AI in five more languages. Beta three is polish, and testers found four changes.\n\nOpen Settings, Battery. The icon finally matches the new one in the corner of your screen.\n\nIn Accessibility, Siri, holding the side button can open Type to Siri again, so you type instead of talking. That's on select models.\n\nUnder Privacy and Security, the Apple Intelligence Report is now called the Private Cloud Compute Report. That's the name of the Apple servers your bigger requests run on.\n\nAnd one tester spotted a silenced icon on pinned chats you've muted in Messages.\n\nSo when do you get it? Apple promised those five Siri languages in October. Its foldable, iPhone Duo, launches October twenty third, and twenty seven point two probably follows soon after.\n\nWaiting on Siri in Spanish or Japanese? Follow, and you'll know the day it lands on your phone.",
